 "note": "Rejected. Across 3 coins x 4 timeframes x 2,592 configurations the paired null clears PF 1.2 at double cost 637 times per seed against the hypothesis's 280, and the null's MEDIAN profit factor is higher than the real market's at 0x, 1x, 2x and 3x cost. The control is as damning: taking every setup the other way scores no worse. And the lever table refutes the mechanism directly - exiting at the VWAP, which is the whole idea, is the single most harmful choice in the grid (median 0.500) while ignoring the VWAP and exiting on time is the best (0.816). The best-looking configurations trade 0.018 times a day, one every two months, which is search noise and fails the phase constraint on its own. This is the same family as the prior repo's dead `VWAP std-band fade`, which backtested at 3.0 and traded at 0.7 on a limit-fill artefact; with honest fills it does not even reach the artefact. One positive: the H-009 crowd gate lifts even this (0.659 to 0.712), a third independent confirmation of that finding.",
